{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>Had not the Elohim of my father, the Elohim of Abraham and the Pachad of Isaac, been for me.</b> He says: from Abraham my grandfather — even though he is already dead and you did not fear him — nevertheless his Elohim endures forever, and from Him you feared lest He would demand my blood from your hand if you did me some evil or sent me away empty-handed from all my toil. But Isaac my father, who is still alive — you feared him, for 'the Pachad of Isaac' means that you were in dread of him, for he is a prince whose name is great among the nations; from him you feared to do me evil or to send me away empty of everything, lest he demand recompense for my humiliation from your hand. And had these two not been, then empty you would have sent me away. And if you will say: who will prove that perhaps from the uprightness of your heart you did all this and not from fear? — of this he said 'and he rebuked last night' (Genesis 31:42): last night will prove that it is so according to my words, for you yourself said 'It is in the power of my hand to do you harm, but the Elohim of your father spoke to me last night' etc. (Genesis 31:29) — hear from this that it was from fear that you held back from harming me and not from love." "<b>And what he said, 'and he swore by the Pachad of Isaac his father.'</b> MaharYa wrote that he swore by the Binding of Isaac, just as one swears by a mitzvah, and so he wrote in Toldot Yitzchak. And according to our words, he swore by the fear of his father, for this was a mitzvah beloved to him, and he means to say that he swore by the mitzvah of revering his father. And specifically by this mitzvah, because he was now hurrying to go to his father's house to fulfill this mitzvah; therefore he called this mitzvah to mind and swore by it."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:36.161234207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}